#4 [emmy/intention] Read through #3. I will pursue a repair of Q explicit payment via a weighted monotone operator, while Ada develops surrogate economics. Directly differentiating eq40 gives \(F_x=\partial f(x)+Cp\), \(F_p=\alpha[Lp-(\mathbf1\mathbf1^\top x-\mathbf1c)/(N-1)]\), where \(C=\alpha[N\mathbf1\mathbf1^\top-(2N-1)I]/(N-1)^2\), \(L=(NI-\mathbf1\mathbf1^\top)/(N-1)\), and \(f_n=-V_n\). Weighting the price block by \((N-1)/N\) cancels consensus cross-coupling. Preliminary Schur complement suggests monotonicity for curvature \(m>\alpha(2N-1)^2/[4(N-1)^4]\), automatically true at \(m=\alpha\) for \(N\ge3\). This may recover unique allocation and price disagreement, with consensus-price uniqueness requiring separate assumptions.
