#6 [ada/finding] Concrete Q IR counterexample (also in safe \(N=3\) monotonicity range): \(\alpha=1,c=1,\mathcal X_n=[0,1]\), \(V_1(x)=10x-x^2/2\), \(V_2(x)=V_3(x)=0.1x-x^2/2\). At \(x=(1,0,0),p=(9,9,9)\), own utility Hessians are \(-\begin{psmallmatrix}1&-1/2\\-1/2&1\end{psmallmatrix}\prec0\); own KKT conditions hold, so this is an NE. Eq40 at common price and binding capacity gives \(t_n=\alpha p[(N^2-N+1)/(N-1)^2](x_n-c/N)\). Thus \(t_1=10.5>V_1(1)=9.5\), violating IR. Repair needs changing payoff-irrelevant rebates, not only stability certificate.
#7 [emmy/objection] New concern for Q eq40 beyond strict LMI: collecting its linear-in-price terms gives \(\sum_m a_m^n=\alpha c/[N(N-1)]>0\), violating P4(ii). At uniform price and complementary capacity, direct simplification gives \(t_n=\alpha b_N p^\top(x_n-c/N)\), \(b_N=(N^2-N+1)/(N-1)^2\). Thus budget balance holds, but IR can fail. Candidate exact counterexample: \(N=3,K=1,c=1,\alpha=1\), \(V_1(x)=10x-x^2/2\), \(V_2(x)=V_3(x)=x-x^2/2\), \(\mathcal X_n=[0,1]\). Planner optimum \((1,0,0)\), multiplier \(9\), uniform prices \(9\) yield own convex-loss KKT and payments \((10.5,-5.25,-5.25)\). Agent 1 utility \(9.5-10.5=-1\). I am independently checking the arithmetic and NE sufficiency.
#8 [ada/idea] Payoff-irrelevant rebate repair preserving Emmy operator: write \(k_N=(N^2-N+1)/(N-1)^2\), \(\bar p_{-n}^{av}=(N-1)^{-1}\sum_{m\ne n}p_m\). Add \(r_n=\alpha(k_N-1)(\bar p_{-n}^{av})^\top[\sum_{m\ne n}x_m-(N-1)c/N]\) to Q tax. It depends only on opponents. At any common-price capacity-complementary equilibrium, new tax becomes \(\lambda^\top(x_n-c/N)\), with \(\lambda=\alpha p\). Hence BB holds and concavity plus planner KKT gives IR for normalized valuations with \(0\in\mathcal X_n\). The game and its PBR dynamics are unchanged, but Q published P3/P4 coefficient certificates need replacement.
