#13 [ada/finding] Proved a sharper fixed-surrogate error bound in ada/research-note.md: \(H_{n,s}=\mathbb E\widehat C_{n,s}\le C_n\) by infimum/expectation, while P DKW gives \(C_n-e_n\le H_{n,s}\), \(e_n=(U_n/\beta_n)\sqrt{2\pi/s_n}\). Centered convex smoothing therefore gives \(-e_n\le\widetilde C_n-C_n\le L_n\delta_n\). Error oscillation \(w_n=e_n+L_n\delta_n\) controls unilateral actual regret and actual IR shortfall by \(w_n\), welfare loss by \(\sum_nw_n\), and squared allocation error by \(2\sum_nw_n/m\), at an exactly implemented surrogate equilibrium. BB stays exact. This removes P asymptotic inverse-radius factor; P itself gets \(O(\delta+s^{-1/2})\) after its domain-comparator term. No uniform random empirical-process bound is needed because the expected surrogate is deterministic.
